    "user_request_original": "Optimize a 36-layer alternating Ta2O5/SiO2 multilayer filter on fused silica substrate with air incidence at 0 degrees, unpolarized light. Initialize thicknesses using quarter-wave conditions: Ta2O5 layers at d=λ_UV/(4*n_Ta2O5)≈39 nm for λ_UV=360 nm, SiO2 layers at d=λ_NIR/(4*n_SiO2)≈176 nm for λ_NIR=1055 nm. Apply alternating sequence starting with Ta2O5. Constrain optimization to ±8 nm Gaussian perturbation around these base values during candidate generation. Layer thickness bounds: 20-350 nm. Optimize for: minimize mean transmittance at 355-365 nm, minimize mean transmittance at 1030-1080 nm, maximize mean transmittance at 420-700 nm. Use gradient_thickness optimizer with bounded noise initialization. Canonical user controls: incidence angles 0 degrees. polarization unpolarized. wavelength intervals 355-355 nm, 355-365 nm, 420-700 nm, 1030-1080 nm. soft objectives: high average transmittance in 420-700 nm; low average transmittance at 355 nm; low average transmittance in 355-365 nm; low average transmittance in 1030-1080 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high transmittance at 355 nm; high transmittance in 355-365 nm; high transmittance in 1030-1080 nm; high loss in 420-700 nm. manufacturing constraints: maximum 36 layers; layer thickness range 20-350 nm.",
